+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  prior: regressed. This is the iteration-1 confirmed finding on the 24 h to 7 d re-issue (§3 window), fixed incompletely: the reset mechanism now exists but does not cover every acknowledgement path.
+  evidence: spec line 79: "success: `SeatTransition::Acknowledge` (seat unchanged), then the invitation reset below"; line 93 defines the reset on "the resurrect success transition".
+  Line 82 (operator resurrect): "the fact reads `Resolved` on the reopened pane: graph acknowledges it as done", with no reset stated; graph made no resurrect call there, so there is no success outcome to carry it.
+  Line 80 (NotFound, then `Resolved`) says "is acknowledged as success"; the refute and ground seats read this as ambiguous, so the lost-response path may be covered by wording.
+  The spec says the poll records settled ordinary invitations as Pending, the channel want counts Pending on the recorded seat as satisfied, and the reset "does not read the window or any clock", so nothing triggers it later.
+  The operator path is the remedy §3 itself prescribes (`herdr-threads seat rebind SEAT --pane PANE --operator`). §6 lists no operator-path or lost-response reset test.
+  fix-shape hint: state that every acknowledgement of a keyless `Retired{Reversible}` Restore seat (own success, NotFound-then-Resolved, operator resurrect, crash recovery) carries the reset in the same journal write, and add an operator-path test.
