+## Rejected (with reason)        ← so re-roasts don't re-litigate
+- §4 table row "adopted (keyless), session captured"; Key decisions ("cooperative continuity is no longer load-bearing for keyless seats"); §6 tier 3 — §4 assumes graph's own relaunch brings a keyless agent back after a cold restart, while Herdr resumes official agents in restored panes by default (`[session] resume_agents_on_restore`), so cooperative continuity usually still places the seat; the spec never mentions Herdr's own resume.
+  reason: rejected 2 to 1. The external premise holds (https://herdr.dev/docs/session-state/: "Native agent session restore is enabled by default"), and all three seats verified it.
+  The §4 Gate already proceeds when the seat is placed "by graph's rebind or anyone else", and the "Accepted behaviour" paragraph covers cooperative continuity placing the seat first.
+  The row text is conditional ("when the rebind succeeds"). A Herdr-resumed agent is present, so graph does not relaunch and continuity places the seat as today.
+  The failure path (a pending continuity claim keeps the rebind at `ServiceBusy`) is the finding's own stated inference; §4.2 retries it and §4.5 surfaces `clones.restart_held` after the grace.
+  Ground seat dissent (CONFIRM, Should-fix): the spec never names Herdr's resume and §6 tier 3 does not test the captured-session path. The majority answers this as a wording and test-coverage suggestion; the ground seat itself calls it "not a design break".
+  Optional follow-up: mention Herdr's own resume in the row and add a tier-3 scenario with default `resume_agents_on_restore`.
