+- Key decisions "what happens to a binding that reconnects later"; §4 table — An old binding or cooperative reattach can contest the rebound seat after graph has launched a fresh agent on it.
+  reason: carried from iteration 1 (rejected 3 to 0); not re-surfaced this round.
+- §3 `replace` paragraph — §3 does not say how graph learns the bare seat to pass as `replace`.
+  reason: carried from iteration 1 (rejected 3 to 0); not re-surfaced this round.
+- §2 "An older daemon refuses the v4 registration … (no silent fallback to v3)" — A daemon older than 3.6.0 takes down all of graph's threads integration.
